 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1787). Words follow the Schirmer vocal score's spelling and punctuation: nostr' alma, bell' idol and quant' io as two words on two notes; oh Dio! (the libretto has oddio!); the print's commas, semicolons and exclamation marks. The first sung syllables, -dele! (bar 1, Don Ottavio), end his Crudele! from the recitative before (Calmatevi, idol mio), so they are left out of the phrases here; Ottavio sings nothing else in this piece. IPA, word meanings and translations were drafted for this app (S56) and the IPA was checked against Castel. In the rondo Anna repeats Non mi dir, Calma il tuo tormento and se di duol non vuoi ch'io mora, and in the Allegretto moderato sings sentirà pietà di me many times; the score's repeats are their own phrases. io is jo where it is sung on one note (bar 29) and ˈi.o where the score gives it two (bars 25, 53); sai is ˈsa.i (two notes). IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
